---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact Us"
  description="How to reach SalaryByCity — data corrections, methodology questions, press, and privacy requests. Direct email, no account or form-wall, typical reply within two business days."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Contact</h1>

    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      We read every message. There's no ticket system to fight through, no account required, and no
      chatbot standing between you and a human — just email. We typically reply within two business
      days, and data-correction reports get priority because accuracy is the entire point of this
      site.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900">
        <h2 class="font-bold">General &amp; data corrections</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          Spotted a number that looks wrong? Include the page URL and, if you can, a source we can
          check against.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:hello@salarybycity.com" class="mt-3 inline-block font-semibold text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">hello@salarybycity.com</a>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900">
        <h2 class="font-bold">Methodology questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          Most answers are already on the <a href="/methodology/" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">methodology page</a> — for anything deeper, write to us.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:data@salarybycity.com" class="mt-3 inline-block font-semibold text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">data@salarybycity.com</a>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900">
        <h2 class="font-bold">Press &amp; citation</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          Journalists and researchers may quote our pages with attribution and a link. We're happy
          to provide context on request.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:press@salarybycity.com" class="mt-3 inline-block font-semibold text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">press@salarybycity.com</a>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-stone-800 dark:bg-stone-900">
        <h2 class="font-bold">Privacy requests</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
          Access, deletion, or opt-out requests under GDPR/CCPA — see our <a href="/privacy/" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:privacy@salarybycity.com" class="mt-3 inline-block font-semibold text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">privacy@salarybycity.com</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Before you write about a salary figure</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      A quick note that saves a round-trip: our numbers are statistical distributions for an
      occupation in a state, not quotes for a specific job. If your offer differs from our median,
      both can be right — the percentile range on each page shows how wide real-world pay runs. But
      if you believe a figure misrepresents the underlying BLS data, that's exactly the kind of
      email we want. Tell us the occupation, the state, the number you expected, and where your
      expectation comes from, and we'll investigate against the source series and reply with what we
      find. Corrections, when warranted, are published in days.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">What we can't help with</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      To set expectations honestly: we are a statistics site, not a career service. We can't review
      your résumé, negotiate on your behalf, connect you with employers or recruiters, or advise on
      your individual tax situation. Requests to buy our traffic, place sponsored content disguised
      as data, or purchase visitor information will be declined — that model is exactly what this
      site was built to avoid.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      And one thing we'll never do with your email: add it to a marketing list, share it with
      recruiters, or use it for anything beyond answering you. We don't sell leads, and there's
      nothing to sign up for — see
      <a href="/about/" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">why we built this site</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
